@startuml 10a_state_move
!include _style.puml
title Tool state machine - Move  (events = ToolEvent, see 04)

state Idle
state Dragging {
  Dragging : data / anchor: CellCoord, offset: (i32, i32), selection_before: Selection, floating: Option<Arc<CellBuffer>>, builder: Option<PatchBuilder>
  Dragging : overlay / MovePreview{ floating, offset }: the floating cells at their offset + the shifted selection outline
}

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [selection empty or !selection.contains(c)]\n/ ignored
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [selection.contains(c), move_mode = Contents, active layer hidden]\n/ Consumed, nothing happens (status bar: Layer is hidden)
Idle --> Dragging : PointerDown(c) [selection.contains(c), move_mode = Contents, active layer visible]\n/ anchor = c; offset = (0, 0); selection_before = selection.clone();\n   floating = extract(active layer, selection); builder.clear(selected cells)  (a hole appears in the layer)
Idle --> Dragging : PointerDown(c) [selection.contains(c), move_mode = OutlineOnly]\n/ anchor = c; offset = (0, 0); no buffer, no builder
Dragging --> Dragging : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ offset = clamp(c - anchor) so that selection.bounds() shifted by offset stays on the page
Dragging --> Dragging : PointerMove(None)\n/ offset unchanged
Dragging --> Idle : PointerUp [offset == (0, 0)]\n/ Contents: builder.rollback()  (nothing recorded)
Dragging --> Idle : PointerUp [offset != (0, 0), Contents]\n/ builder.blit(floating, offset); selection.translate(offset);\n   history.record_applied_with_selection(builder.finish("Move cells"), SelectionChange)
Dragging --> Idle : PointerUp [offset != (0, 0), OutlineOnly]\n/ selection.translate(offset)  (selection is not undoable)
Dragging --> Idle : Key(Escape) | Cancel | Deactivate\n/ Contents: builder.rollback(); drag = None; selection unchanged
Idle --> Idle : Key(Arrow*) [selection non-empty]\n/ one nudge of 1 cell (Shift = 10) = the PointerUp logic with offset = delta (clamped to the page)
Idle --> Idle : Key / DoubleClick [otherwise]\n/ Ignored

note bottom
  Contents mode: the selected cells of the ACTIVE layer (both planes) are lifted, the layer shows a hole while dragging, and on release the cells are
  written at the new place. Only cells that hold something overwrite the destination (blit rule); the cells left behind are empty.
  The whole drag is ONE undo step, and undo also puts the selection back where it was.
  The offset is clamped so that no selected cell can leave the page: nothing is ever lost at the border.
  Outline only: just the marching ants move (no layer data changes, nothing to undo).
  is_busy() is true in Dragging. Undo / redo always send Cancel first, which rolls a running drag back.
end note
@enduml

@startuml 10b_state_stroke_tools
!include _style.puml
title Tool state machine - Paint and Erase  (StrokeTool<O>, O = PaintOperation | EraseOperation)

state Idle
Idle : data / hover: Option<CellCoord>   (drives the brush footprint outline)
state Stroking
Stroking : data / last: CellCoord, builder: PatchBuilder (active layer)

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Idle : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ hover = Some(c)
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [active layer hidden]\n/ Consumed, nothing happens (status bar: Layer is hidden)
Idle --> Stroking : PointerDown(c)\n/ builder = new(frame id, active layer id); last = c;\n   op.stamp(c)  (checks selection.permits per target cell, writes the planes switched on)
Stroking --> Stroking : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ for k in line(last, c) skipping last: op.stamp(k); last = c; hover = c
Stroking --> Stroking : PointerMove(None)\n/ ignored (pointer left the page; last unchanged)
Stroking --> Idle : PointerUp(_)\n/ commit()
Stroking --> Idle : Cancel | Deactivate\n/ commit()
Idle --> Idle : Key\n/ Ignored

note bottom
  commit() = if let Some(cmd) = builder.finish(op.label()) { history.record_applied(cmd) }.
  A stroke that changed nothing (e.g. painting a cell with the value it already has, or no plane switched on) records NOTHING.
  One continuous drag = one undo step, even when it crosses many cells.
  Paint stamps the active brush (glyph cells only) on every cell of the stroke: planes.foreground writes glyph + char colour, planes.background writes the fill colour.
  Erase clears an erase_size x erase_size square: planes.foreground -> empty glyph, planes.background -> transparent fill.
  Active selection: target cells outside the selection are skipped per cell, the stroke itself keeps running.
end note
@enduml

@startuml 10c_state_fill
!include _style.puml
title Tool state machine - Fill  (stateless: every click is atomic)

state Idle

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [active layer hidden]\n/ Consumed, nothing happens (status bar: Layer is hidden)
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [selection non-empty and !selection.contains(c)]\n/ ignored
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [no plane switched on, or in every switched-on plane the seed already holds the target value]\n/ nothing to do, nothing recorded
Idle --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [otherwise]\n/ for EACH plane in options.planes: cells = FloodFill::region(active layer, c, plane, &selection);\n   one PatchBuilder: Foreground -> InkCell{glyph: brush.fill_glyph(), color: ink}, Background -> fill_color;\n   history.record_applied(builder.finish("Fill cells"))
Idle --> Idle : PointerMove / PointerUp / Key / Cancel / Deactivate\n/ Ignored

note bottom
  The fill is computed and applied entirely inside the PointerDown handler (4-connected scanline fill, max 17 280 cells per plane at the default canvas).
  The two planes are filled INDEPENDENTLY: the foreground region is bounded by differences in glyph / character colour, the background region only by
  differences in fill colour, and neither looks at other layers. With both planes on, two regions are written in one undo step.
  There is no preview and no drag behaviour.
end note
@enduml

@startuml 10d_state_shape_select
!include _style.puml
title Tool state machine - Square select and Ellipse select  (ShapeSelectTool<RectShape | EllipseShape>)

state Idle
state Dragging {
  Dragging : data / anchor: CellCoord, current: CellCoord, mode: SelectionMode
  Dragging : overlay / RectPreview or EllipsePreview of CellRect::from_corners(anchor, current)
}

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Dragging : PointerDown(c, mods)\n/ drag = {anchor: c, current: c, mode: options.mode_for(mods)}
Dragging --> Dragging : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ current = c
Dragging --> Dragging : PointerMove(None)\n/ current = clamp(last known pointer position to the page)
Dragging --> Idle : PointerUp(_)\n/ cells = shape.rasterize(anchor, current, spec);\n   selection.apply(cells, mode)
Dragging --> Idle : Key(Escape) | Cancel | Deactivate\n/ drag = None  (selection unchanged)

note bottom
  mode: a held Alt = Subtract, a held Shift = Add, otherwise the Replace / Add / Subtract button of the top bar. The modifier is read ONCE at PointerDown.
  A click without moving selects the single cell under the pointer (anchor == current -> 1 x 1 shape).
end note
@enduml

@startuml 10e_state_polygon_select
!include _style.puml
title Tool state machine - Polygon select  (SelectPolygonTool)

state Idle
state Building {
  Building : data / vertices: Vec<CellCoord> (n >= 1), hover: Option<CellCoord>, mode: SelectionMode
  Building : overlay / PolygonPreview(vertices, hover, mode): edges between vertices + rubber-band edge to hover
}

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Building : PointerDown(c, mods)\n/ vertices = [c]; mode = options.mode_for(mods)
Building --> Building : PointerDown(c) [c == last vertex]\n/ ignored (absorbs the 2nd click of a double-click)
Building --> Building : PointerDown(c) [c == vertices[0] and n < 3]\n/ ignored
Building --> Building : PointerDown(c) [otherwise, not closing]\n/ vertices.push(c)
Building --> Building : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ hover = Some(c)
Building --> Building : Key(Backspace) [n > 1]\n/ vertices.pop()
Building --> Idle : Key(Backspace) [n == 1]\n/ vertices.clear()
Building --> Idle : PointerDown(c) [c == vertices[0] and n >= 3]\n/ close()
Building --> Idle : DoubleClick | Key(Enter)\n/ close()
Building --> Idle : Key(Escape) | Cancel | Deactivate\n/ vertices.clear() (selection unchanged)

note bottom
  close(): if n < 3 -> vertices.clear() (nothing selected).
          else cells = ShapeRasterizer::polygon(vertices, spec); selection.apply(cells, mode); vertices.clear().
  The polygon is closed automatically from the last vertex back to the first. Vertices sit at cell CENTRES.
  The selection mode (Alt / Shift / top bar button) is read at the FIRST click only.
  is_busy() is true in Building. Undo / redo always send Cancel first, which discards the polygon.
end note
@enduml

@startuml 10f_state_pick
!include _style.puml
title Tool state machine - Pick (colour picker)  (never writes into the project)

state Idle
Idle : data / hover: Option<CellCoord>
state Sampling
Sampling : data / hover: CellCoord   (primary button held: dragging scrubs through cells)

[*] --> Idle
Idle --> Idle : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ hover = Some(c)   (overlay: one-cell outline)
Idle --> Sampling : PointerDown(c)\n/ sample(c) -> ToolResponse::Picked(PickedColors)
Sampling --> Sampling : PointerMove(Some(c))\n/ hover = c; sample(c) -> ToolResponse::Picked(PickedColors)
Sampling --> Sampling : PointerMove(None)\n/ ignored
Sampling --> Idle : PointerUp(_) | Cancel | Deactivate\n/ nothing to commit
Idle --> Idle : Key / DoubleClick\n/ Ignored

note bottom
  sample(c), driven by options.planes (the paint mode) and options.pick_source:
    planes.foreground -> ink  = character colour at c    (Merged: Compositor::flatten_cell(...).ink when it has a glyph | ActiveLayer: the layer's ink colour when it has a glyph)
    planes.background -> fill = background colour at c   (Merged: flatten_cell(...).fill when its alpha > 0 | ActiveLayer: the layer's fill colour when its alpha > 0)
  A plane with nothing at c yields None (that colour is left alone, status bar: No character here / No background here).
  The caller applies the answer: EditorSession::apply_picked sets ink_color / fill_color. Colours keep their alpha. The glyph / brush is never picked.
  Picking is not undoable and does not make the project dirty. The selection does not restrict it. is_busy() is always false.
end note
@enduml
